<title>USA: Wet Seal sees Q2 profit around $0.25/shr.</title>
<headline>Wet Seal sees Q2 profit around $0.25/shr.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wet Seal Inc on Thursday said it expects to report a second quarter profit of about $0.25 a share for the period ended August 2, compared to earnings of $0.25 per share a year ago.</p>
<p>In a statement, the fashion retailer said sales for the second quarter of fiscal 1997 were $94.3 million compared to sales of $94.4 million a year ago.</p>
</text>
